@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="container mt-4">
    <h1>About Finance Tracker</h1>

    <div class="row mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-8">
            <h3>What is Finance Tracker?</h3>
            <p>
                Finance Tracker is a personal finance management application that helps you track your spending,
                manage your deposits, and visualize your financial health. Whether you are saving for a specific good
                or just want to understand where your money goes, this tool makes it easy to stay on top of your finances.
            </p>

            <h3 class="mt-4">Key Features</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Transaction Tracking:</strong> Record and categorize all your expenses</li>
                <li><strong>Deposit Management:</strong>Track income from various sources</li>
                <li><strong>Dashboard Overview:</strong>See your total spending, deposits, and remaining balance</li>
                <li><strong>Visual Charts:</strong>View spending breakdowns by category</li>
                <li><strong>Progress Tracking:</strong>Monitor how much of your budget has been spent</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="mt-4">How to Use Finance Tracker</h3>

            <h4>Getting Started</h4>
            <ol>
                <li>Start by adding your initial deposits using the "Deposits" section</li>
                <li>Record your regular expenses as transactions</li>
                <li>View your dashboard to see your financial overview</li>
            </ol>

            <h4>Managing Deposits</h4>
            <ol>
                <li>Go to the "Deposits" page from the navbr</li>
                <li>Click "Add New Deposit"</li>
                <li>Enter the date, description, amount, and form of money</li>
                <li>Click "Create" to save your deposit</li>
            </ol>

            <h4>Viewing your dashboard</h4>
            <p>
                The home page displays your finnancial summary including total deposits, total spent,
                remaining balance, and a chart showing spending by category. This helps you quickly
                understand your finnancial situation at a glance.
            </p>

            <h3 class="mt-4">Technical Information</h3>
            <p>
                <strong>Version:</strong> 1.0<br />
                <strong>Technology Stack:</strong> ASP.Net Core, SQL Server, Entity Framework Core<br />
                <strong>System Requirements:</strong> Modern web browser with JavaScript enabled
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="card-header">
                <h5>Quick Tips</h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <ul>
                    <li>Regularly update your transactions for accurate tracking</li>
                    <li>Use categories to organize your spending</li>
                    <li>Check your dashboard frequently to monitor progress</li>
                    <li>Set aside time each week to review your finances</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card mt-3">
            <div class="card-header">
                <h5>Need Help?</h5>
            </div>
            <div class="card-body">
                <p>
                    If you have questions or encounter issues, please visit our
                    <a asp-action="Contact">Contact</a> page for assistance.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
